1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,833
<i> We move for the grant of bail.</i>

2
00:00:01,967 --> 00:00:03,667
<i>Just earlier, there was
an attempt on his life.</i>

3
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,433
<i> Motion for bail is denied.</i>

4
00:00:05,567 --> 00:00:07,967
<i>The accused shall be committed
to the provincial jail,</i>

5
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,267
<i>effective immediately,
pending trial.</i>

6
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,800
<i>Who was with you earlier
at your house?</i>

7
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:13,300
<i> I know someone's helping you!</i>

8
00:00:13,433 --> 00:00:14,267
<i> If he didn't escape,</i>

9
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,500
<i>that means the syndicate
took him.</i>

10
00:00:16,633 --> 00:00:18,533
<i>If you're hiding something,
tell us.</i>

11
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,733
<i> I really regret</i>

12
00:00:19,867 --> 00:00:22,067
<i>getting involved
with your syndicate!</i>

13
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,067
<i>There is still no confirmation
on Major Aglipay's whereabouts</i>

14
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,400
<i> following the incident.</i>

15
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:27,700
<i> Is this about Diego?</i>

16
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:29,700
<i>Miguel Cruz needs to know
about this.</i>

17
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:32,200
<i>The Major's arraignment
hearing just ended.</i>

18
00:00:32,333 --> 00:00:34,333
<i> He wasn't granted bail.</i>

19
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,467
<i> What?</i>

20
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,367
<i>I'm the holdup man
you wouldn't stop chasing</i>

21
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,600
<i> until I ended up in jail.</i>

22
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:39,700
<i> Hey! What's that?</i>

23
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:40,933
<i> Just fooling around.</i>

24
00:00:41,067 --> 00:00:43,367
<i>Maybe you can expose
what really happened.</i>

25
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,867
<i> Joey, we need solid evidence</i>

26
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,133
<i> against the syndicates.</i>

27
00:00:47,267 --> 00:00:49,200
<i>You don't really care
about my father!</i>

28
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:50,433
<i> All you care about</i>

29
00:00:50,567 --> 00:00:52,267
<i>are your subscribers
and your show!</i>

30
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,233
<i>I've seen groups like the one
Diego got involved with.</i>

31
00:00:55,367 --> 00:00:57,100
<i> They make people disappear.</i>

32
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,200
<i> No one ever finds them.</i>

33
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:01,400
<i>You're saying he's really gone?</i>

34
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:21,400
Every day riding hard,

35
00:01:21,533 --> 00:01:24,300
Fearless speeding ahead!

36
00:01:25,167 --> 00:01:26,433
Bullseye!

37
00:01:27,033 --> 00:01:29,800
We stay sharp every day,
our fellow tiradas.

38
00:01:29,933 --> 00:01:31,433
No more beating around the bush.

39
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:33,133
Straight to it!

40
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:40,533
We're on it.

41
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,433
We'll keep investigating.

42
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:48,067
It's the same script over
and over from the police.

43
00:01:48,933 --> 00:01:51,100
A whole day has passed

44
00:01:51,233 --> 00:01:53,800
have they identified
the syndicate

45
00:01:53,933 --> 00:01:56,467
that broke into
Major Aglipay's house?

46
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:58,467
And are they connected

47
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,767
to other drug cases
in Metro Manila

48
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:04,000
And the biggest question,
our "ka-Tirada"...

49
00:02:05,133 --> 00:02:08,500
Where is Major Aglipay?

50
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,367
Is there an answer?

51
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,000
None.

52
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,133
Nothing.

53
00:02:17,667 --> 00:02:18,833
Our fellow tiradas...

54
00:02:19,833 --> 00:02:24,433
This is how brazen these
syndicates have become.

55
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:26,367
And our police?

56
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:28,200
Just chilling.

57
00:02:28,333 --> 00:02:30,167
But when everything is exposed,

58
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:31,833
I promise you

59
00:02:31,967 --> 00:02:35,400
<i> heads will roll,</i>

60
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:40,000
<i>and those who should lose their
positions will be go.</i>

61
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,567
We'll be back.

62
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:45,600
We'll be back, our "ka-Tirada."

63
00:02:47,967 --> 00:02:49,200
Cue commercial.

64
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:51,100
Three, two, one, and...

65
00:02:55,267 --> 00:02:57,600
He's back!

66
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:03,600
Boss Idol!

67
00:03:03,733 --> 00:03:06,900
Boss Idol! Boss Idol!

68
00:03:07,033 --> 00:03:09,233
They'll never find the cop...

69
00:03:09,367 --> 00:03:12,367
because he's already being eaten
by tawilis.

70
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:14,100
Right, Matias?

71
00:03:14,633 --> 00:03:16,767
They've been feeding people
to them for a long time.

72
00:03:17,367 --> 00:03:19,400
Anyone who goes against us...

73
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,133
ends up the same way.

74
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,533
But we can't just keep doing
damage control.

75
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:28,167
We won't run out of enemies.

76
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:30,400
That's why we have
to be proactive.

77
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:31,767
What do you mean?

78
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:33,867
We still have a lot
of loose ends.

79
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,367
That's why we have to control
the narrative

80
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:39,100
before the truth
about Diego comes out.

81
00:03:39,233 --> 00:03:40,433
They might use it

82
00:03:40,567 --> 00:03:42,833
to clear Delgado's name.

83
00:03:43,633 --> 00:03:45,867
I think I know what you need.

84
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:56,800
Jin Ho, that's the name
of the one who brought you home?

85
00:03:57,600 --> 00:04:01,167
Why am I only hearing
that name now?

86
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:03,900
He's a new boarder

87
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:05,667
at the boarding school, Mom.

88
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,467
We just became friends recently,

89
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:09,533
and he hangs out with Peter.

90
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:16,767
Joey, I spoke
with your father's lawyer.

91
00:04:17,167 --> 00:04:19,033
He said...

92
00:04:19,167 --> 00:04:23,700
we no longer have any chance
to appeal the bail decision.

93
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:27,733
So that mean

94
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,500
Dad will really stay
in the provincial jail

95
00:04:29,633 --> 00:04:31,500
while his case is being heard?

96
00:04:34,067 --> 00:04:36,100
You know, in times like this,

97
00:04:36,233 --> 00:04:39,967
your Godfather Diego's advice
would have helped.

98
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:43,700
But now...

99
00:04:44,567 --> 00:04:45,667
He's missing.

100
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:49,633
We don't even know if he's safe.

101
00:04:51,733 --> 00:04:54,800
But you know,
when he visited me here,

102
00:04:54,933 --> 00:04:56,433
he said goodbye, because...

103
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,667
he said he was being assigned
somewhere else.

104
00:05:02,267 --> 00:05:03,733
Mom, there's something
you need to know

105
00:05:03,867 --> 00:05:05,300
about Godfather Diego.

106
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,667
Dad...

107
00:05:21,733 --> 00:05:23,100
Joey...

108
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:25,300
You're safe.

109
00:05:33,367 --> 00:05:35,067
Clarissa...

110
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,667
I know everything.

111
00:05:55,267 --> 00:05:56,767
About Diego.

112
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:00,433
About how he betrayed you.

113
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:05,800
About planting the gun
in your car.

114
00:06:08,233 --> 00:06:10,333
And his connection to the...

115
00:06:10,467 --> 00:06:12,800
syndicate that set you up.

116
00:06:14,033 --> 00:06:15,867
Miguel, I know everything.

117
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:17,967
<i> This is for you.</i>

118
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,367
<i>- No, no, no!
- Take it.</i>

119
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,933
<i>- No, no.
- Keep it, use it.</i>

120
00:06:21,067 --> 00:06:21,867
<i> It's just payment</i>

121
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
<i>for all the wrongs I did to you.</i>

122
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,767
So that's why he asked
for forgiveness.

123
00:06:28,033 --> 00:06:31,833
That's why he said he did
everything to protect you.

124
00:06:33,567 --> 00:06:35,400
If only I had
clarified things...

125
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:41,100
maybe something
would've changed.

126
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,867
Maybe he wouldn't have
disappeared.

127
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,033
Maybe you would've been
freed too.

128
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,033
You're not at fault, Clarissa.

129
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,800
Does that mean...

130
00:06:57,133 --> 00:07:00,000
you believe I didn't do
anything wrong?

131
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,033
That I was set up

132
00:07:03,167 --> 00:07:04,700
and I didn't kill anyone?

133
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:08,833
Miguel, I know you're not
capable of killing someone.

134
00:07:10,767 --> 00:07:13,433
We can't deny that...

135
00:07:15,967 --> 00:07:17,933
our relationship had cracks long

136
00:07:18,067 --> 00:07:20,100
before all this happened.

137
00:07:24,833 --> 00:07:27,433
But I will support you
in your case.

138
00:07:34,533 --> 00:07:35,867
When this is all over

139
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,800
when I'm free...

140
00:07:39,367 --> 00:07:41,500
I'll make it up to all of you.

141
00:07:57,433 --> 00:07:58,600
Miguel.

142
00:07:58,733 --> 00:08:00,200
Attorney.

143
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:03,033
There's something
you need to know.

144
00:08:12,967 --> 00:08:15,000
<i>Major Aglipay
was always generous.</i>

145
00:08:15,967 --> 00:08:18,000
<i>Often treated everyone
at the precinct.</i>

146
00:08:18,133 --> 00:08:19,567
<i> We always wondered</i>

147
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,700
<i>where his money was coming from.</i>

148
00:08:22,233 --> 00:08:24,233
<i> Now I know.</i>

149
00:08:27,867 --> 00:08:30,367
<i>A sports car,
a mansion in Tagaytay,</i>

150
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,100
<i> and a farm in Zambales.</i>

151
00:08:32,233 --> 00:08:33,200
<i> Just a few properties</i>

152
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:36,033
<i>discovered under
Major Diego Aglipay's name.</i>

153
00:08:36,167 --> 00:08:37,567
<i> The question many are asking,</i>

154
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:40,367
<i>can a police major really
afford all that?</i>

155
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,000
<i> Sources say he wasn't alone</i>

156
00:08:42,133 --> 00:08:43,700
<i> in this drug operation.</i>

157
00:08:43,833 --> 00:08:45,733
<i> Names have surfaced</i>

158
00:08:45,867 --> 00:08:47,200
<i> Major Miguel Delgado</i>

159
00:08:47,333 --> 00:08:49,467
<i>of the Bolagos Provincial
Police.</i>

160
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,467
<i> Police academy batchmate.</i>

161
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,133
<i> Best friends in life.</i>

162
00:08:53,267 --> 00:08:56,400
<i>That's the story of Major
Delgado and Major Aglipay.</i>

163
00:08:56,567 --> 00:08:58,833
<i>Twelve years later,
Major Aglipay,</i>

164
00:08:58,967 --> 00:09:00,233
<i> missing because of drugs.</i>

165
00:09:00,367 --> 00:09:03,667
<i>Delgado, jailed
because of drugs.</i>

166
00:09:04,167 --> 00:09:06,133
<i> From brothers-in-arms</i>

167
00:09:06,267 --> 00:09:09,367
<i> to brothers-in-crime?</i>

168
00:09:09,967 --> 00:09:12,767
What if Major Delgado
is really guilty?

169
00:09:14,533 --> 00:09:18,933
<i>It's not impossible he was also
protecting the syndicate...</i>

170
00:09:20,767 --> 00:09:22,533
just like his best friend.

171
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:27,700
<i>I thought you were
a good person!</i>

172
00:09:27,867 --> 00:09:29,533
<i>I thought you were going
to help Dad!</i>

173
00:09:29,667 --> 00:09:31,833
<i>But you're the reason
he's in jail!</i>

174
00:09:31,967 --> 00:09:33,567
<i> They don't need to see you.</i>

175
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:36,233
<i>Even if you hide,
they'll find you.</i>

176
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:37,567
<i> You don't know these people.</i>

177
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:39,433
<i>Because you're the one
they know?</i>

178
00:09:39,567 --> 00:09:42,267
<i>Because they're the syndicate
and they want you dead?</i>

179
00:09:44,133 --> 00:09:46,900
Andrew, be careful.

180
00:09:47,033 --> 00:09:49,733
Maybe Major Delgado
is just playing you.

181
00:09:50,233 --> 00:09:51,667
Don't be fooled.

182
00:09:53,667 --> 00:09:55,133
Elai, you know me.

183
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,233
I have the knack
to read through people's faces

184
00:09:58,367 --> 00:10:00,900
whether they're telling
the truth or not.

185
00:10:01,933 --> 00:10:04,267
And I always stand
with the truth.

186
00:10:06,167 --> 00:10:08,700
That's why I don't need
to clear or destroy

187
00:10:08,833 --> 00:10:10,967
Major Delgado's name.

188
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:13,300
because I'm just always
after the truth.

189
00:10:14,367 --> 00:10:17,033
What do you really know
about Major Delgado?

190
00:10:17,167 --> 00:10:18,833
Why won't you release it?

191
00:10:24,733 --> 00:10:27,133
I won't unleash a flood

192
00:10:27,267 --> 00:10:28,633
until I know exactly

193
00:10:28,767 --> 00:10:31,833
who deserves to drown
in their own mud.

194
00:10:31,967 --> 00:10:33,967
Talk to your
field correspondents.

195
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:36,733
Find out where the information

196
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:40,500
about Major Aglipay
is coming from.

197
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,100
Go, Kyle, on it.

198
00:10:44,233 --> 00:10:45,767
Copy.

199
00:10:50,633 --> 00:10:51,767
They're being so unfair.

200
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:54,167
Just because Dad and Godfather
Diego are best friends,

201
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:56,867
they're already saying
they're accomplices?

202
00:10:58,133 --> 00:11:01,467
That's the ongoing narrative
on social media

203
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,600
and even in mainstream media.

204
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,100
All of it, Attorney?

205
00:11:07,233 --> 00:11:09,200
Doesn't that seem suspicious?

206
00:11:09,967 --> 00:11:12,000
I'm sure someone's
manipulating this.

207
00:11:13,133 --> 00:11:15,033
They're forcing the blame on me.

208
00:11:16,233 --> 00:11:17,733
Your time is up.

209
00:11:18,833 --> 00:11:21,567
Sir, we're just discussing
something important.

210
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:22,933
They can come back another time.

211
00:11:23,067 --> 00:11:24,700
Let's go.

212
00:11:27,767 --> 00:11:29,267
Clarissa...

213
00:11:29,767 --> 00:11:31,167
Joey, my child...

214
00:11:31,633 --> 00:11:32,633
Be careful.

215
00:11:32,767 --> 00:11:35,067
Don't trust anyone.

216
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:15,433
So much has happened today.

217
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,100
Thank you, Mom.

218
00:12:17,233 --> 00:12:18,433
First...

219
00:12:18,567 --> 00:12:20,300
the person we trusted

220
00:12:20,433 --> 00:12:21,733
your Godfather Diego...

221
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:24,400
turned out to be a traitor.

222
00:12:24,533 --> 00:12:28,233
Instead of helping
your father get released,

223
00:12:28,367 --> 00:12:30,533
he only got himself dragged
deeper into this.

224
00:12:32,967 --> 00:12:35,767
How are we supposed to help
your father now?

225
00:12:36,467 --> 00:12:37,867
Especially when we don't
even know

226
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,467
who we can trust anymore.

227
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,867
That's exactly it, Mom.

228
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,800
Even the video
I was holding on to

229
00:12:43,933 --> 00:12:46,033
the one I believed
could help Dad

230
00:12:46,167 --> 00:12:48,467
I don't even know
where it is now.

231
00:12:49,667 --> 00:12:51,433
My child...

232
00:12:51,933 --> 00:12:54,867
Stop chasing that video.

233
00:12:55,567 --> 00:12:57,100
You saw what happened

234
00:12:57,233 --> 00:12:59,000
to your Godfather Diego,
didn't you?

235
00:12:59,133 --> 00:13:01,367
Your father is already in jail.

236
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:03,233
I couldn't bear it

237
00:13:03,367 --> 00:13:05,633
if something happened
to you too.

238
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,567
Please, enough.

239
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:15,100
Let it go.

240
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:26,100
Cheers.

241
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:29,967
That's what everyone's
talking about now.

242
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:33,500
The cop and Delgado,
partners in crime.

243
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:36,533
How did you put
all that together?

244
00:13:36,667 --> 00:13:37,900
Easy.

245
00:13:38,033 --> 00:13:39,600
A little twist to the story,

246
00:13:39,733 --> 00:13:41,000
a drizzle of drama,

247
00:13:41,133 --> 00:13:42,533
and done.

248
00:13:42,667 --> 00:13:46,633
People love scandal
more than the facts, Matias.

249
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,400
Come to think of it,

250
00:13:48,533 --> 00:13:50,467
no one even bothers to research.

251
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:53,633
Even without proof,
as long as it's catchy,

252
00:13:53,767 --> 00:13:55,267
people will swallow it whole.

253
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:57,000
Exactly.

254
00:13:57,133 --> 00:14:00,167
And of course, credits
to Tomas's PR team

255
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:03,967
for gathering content creators,
influencers,

256
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:07,767
even journalists
to spread the fake news.

257
00:14:09,867 --> 00:14:11,567
It's a great story.

258
00:14:12,033 --> 00:14:15,200
Romance turned crime duo.

259
00:14:16,333 --> 00:14:17,967
Perfect for a primetime
drama series.

260
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:23,400
So, Tomas, isn't it fun
to play the puppet master?

261
00:14:23,533 --> 00:14:26,200
You know, to play god?

262
00:14:29,933 --> 00:14:32,033
Cheers.

263
00:14:47,967 --> 00:14:50,833
Move!
Acting like you own the place!

264
00:14:51,233 --> 00:14:52,867
The place's wide enough!

265
00:14:53,867 --> 00:14:56,100
I'll walk wherever I want!

266
00:14:56,233 --> 00:14:58,600
You think we're scared of you...

267
00:14:58,733 --> 00:15:00,933
just because you're part
of a syndicate, huh?

268
00:15:01,867 --> 00:15:03,367
I'm not in a syndicate.

269
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:05,667
Not in a syndicate...

270
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:06,867
Who are you fooling?

271
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,500
Inside and outside prison,

272
00:15:08,633 --> 00:15:11,133
you and your abusive best friend
are all anyone talks about.

273
00:15:11,267 --> 00:15:12,467
Oh...

274
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:14,133
You wanna fight?

275
00:15:14,267 --> 00:15:15,300
What?

276
00:15:15,433 --> 00:15:18,600
Want the criminals you locked up
in here to swarm you?

277
00:15:19,067 --> 00:15:20,333
There are a lot of us!

278
00:15:20,467 --> 00:15:22,633
We can tear you apart!

279
00:15:25,533 --> 00:15:28,600
And if you think you can ask
the guards for help,

280
00:15:28,733 --> 00:15:29,900
forget it.

281
00:15:30,033 --> 00:15:31,433
Remember...

282
00:15:31,567 --> 00:15:33,333
you killed one of their own!

283
00:15:33,467 --> 00:15:34,500
Huh?

284
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:36,767
You think they'll side with you?

285
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:38,267
No!

286
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,800
You're going to rot in here!

287
00:15:42,133 --> 00:15:43,133
Isn't that right?

288
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:46,967
What? Isn't that right?

289
00:15:49,233 --> 00:15:50,967
You're going to rot in here!

290
00:15:55,900 --> 00:15:57,667
You want to fight?

291
00:16:10,567 --> 00:16:11,800
So...

292
00:16:11,933 --> 00:16:14,033
Are you gonna do
what your mother told you?

293
00:16:15,133 --> 00:16:16,467
Are you giving up?

294
00:16:17,933 --> 00:16:19,233
Not now.

295
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:23,200
Not now when they're tightening
the noose around Dad even more.

296
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:25,500
He needs our help.

297
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:30,567
Joey, we all know Uncle Miguel
is a good man.

298
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,100
But the question is,
how do we prove that?

299
00:16:37,467 --> 00:16:39,767
I know someone who can help me.

300
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,300
We just need to find her.

301
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:44,267
Who?

302
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:46,133
Who are we looking for?

303
00:16:51,367 --> 00:16:52,300
Hi, Sir!

304
00:16:52,433 --> 00:16:53,767
Facial or massage?

305
00:16:54,167 --> 00:16:55,767
Ah, neither.

306
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:58,133
I'm actually here
'cause I'm looking for someone,

307
00:16:58,267 --> 00:17:00,167
It's Golda.

308
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:02,467
She used to run this place,
I think.

309
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,533
Oh, Golda...

310
00:17:04,667 --> 00:17:05,900
Doesn't sound familiar,

311
00:17:06,033 --> 00:17:07,133
but I run this place now.

312
00:17:07,267 --> 00:17:08,567
I'm the owner.

313
00:17:09,467 --> 00:17:11,267
You are the owner?

314
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,467
Yes.

315
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,200
Or maybe the manager?

316
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:16,600
- Owner, yes.
- Oh...

317
00:17:16,767 --> 00:17:20,200
Ah, but, have you
at least met Golda?

318
00:17:20,333 --> 00:17:22,133
Have you heard about her?

319
00:17:22,267 --> 00:17:23,833
I'm not familiar with her

320
00:17:23,967 --> 00:17:27,200
and we actually value
our privacy here.

321
00:17:27,333 --> 00:17:29,233
So if you don't need
any services, Sir,

322
00:17:29,367 --> 00:17:31,000
you may leave now.

323
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:32,367
Thank you.

324
00:17:32,833 --> 00:17:34,467
- Right.
- Mrs. Martinez.

325
00:17:35,133 --> 00:17:36,267
Please come in.

326
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:39,067
Thank you, thank you,
sorry for the trouble.

327
00:17:43,667 --> 00:17:45,067
So...

328
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:48,267
This Golda,
she was an informant,

329
00:17:48,433 --> 00:17:51,100
but not listed
in any official record?

330
00:17:51,533 --> 00:17:52,800
Yes.

331
00:17:52,933 --> 00:17:54,733
That's why they used her
against him.

332
00:18:09,967 --> 00:18:13,200
And she's still here
after betraying a policeman?

333
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:16,733
We're not sure.

334
00:18:16,867 --> 00:18:18,500
That's why we're checking,
right?

335
00:18:19,767 --> 00:18:21,367
That's the place.

336
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:26,367
You again?

337
00:18:27,067 --> 00:18:29,267
You two again?

338
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:32,233
What are you doing here?

339
00:18:32,367 --> 00:18:33,700
Isn't it obvious?

340
00:18:34,167 --> 00:18:35,867
We're looking for Golda.

341
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:38,100
You probably know that my father
is being further implicated

342
00:18:38,233 --> 00:18:40,400
because of the accusations
against Uncle Diego, right?

343
00:18:40,867 --> 00:18:42,100
Golda is the only one
who can prove

344
00:18:42,233 --> 00:18:43,600
those allegations aren't true.

345
00:18:44,333 --> 00:18:45,667
I know.

346
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:47,867
Same reason why I am here.

347
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:50,633
Why?

348
00:18:50,767 --> 00:18:52,500
You're still going to help us

349
00:18:52,633 --> 00:18:54,367
even after I snapped at you?

350
00:18:55,933 --> 00:19:01,100
Joey, the truth matters more
to me than your tantrums.

351
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:04,467
But...

352
00:19:05,167 --> 00:19:06,800
we won't get anything
from inside.

353
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,367
I talked to a woman.

354
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:10,600
She clearly knows something,

355
00:19:10,733 --> 00:19:13,467
but her lips are sealed.

356
00:19:15,133 --> 00:19:16,100
Wait, wait.

357
00:19:16,233 --> 00:19:17,900
English, please.

358
00:19:19,167 --> 00:19:22,300
I said I got nothing inside.

359
00:19:23,167 --> 00:19:24,933
They are hiding Golda.

360
00:19:25,967 --> 00:19:27,333
Ah...

361
00:19:27,467 --> 00:19:30,733
So you just don't have
the finesse, huh?

362
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:31,700
I'll handle it.

363
00:19:31,833 --> 00:19:33,300
Let me try.

364
00:19:36,167 --> 00:19:37,733
- Hi.
- Yes, Sir?

365
00:19:37,867 --> 00:19:40,033
Ah, I'm looking for Golda.

366
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:42,067
Wait, Sir.

367
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,333
I will call my manager.

368
00:19:43,467 --> 00:19:45,033
Oh...

369
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,567
- Hi, Sir.
- Hi!

370
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:02,067
Facial or massage?

371
00:20:02,233 --> 00:20:03,867
Oh, you know...

372
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,600
I'm looking for Golda

373
00:20:05,733 --> 00:20:08,300
because she used to do
my facials.

374
00:20:08,433 --> 00:20:09,900
You know...

375
00:20:11,167 --> 00:20:14,533
Her hand was so gentle...

376
00:20:14,667 --> 00:20:16,267
much like yours.

377
00:20:17,833 --> 00:20:19,700
Golda? Oh...

378
00:20:19,833 --> 00:20:22,500
She doesn't work here anymore,
but we're cousins.

379
00:20:22,633 --> 00:20:24,433
Cousins? Really?

380
00:20:24,567 --> 00:20:26,667
That's why we have
the same soft hands.

381
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:29,267
That's why
you're beautiful both.

382
00:20:29,867 --> 00:20:31,133
Thank you.

383
00:20:31,767 --> 00:20:34,567
But for me, you know,

384
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:36,167
just between us...

385
00:20:38,167 --> 00:20:40,200
you're the beautiful one.

386
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:41,900
Thank you.

387
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,867
But you know,
Golda trained me herself.

388
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,800
So, whatever she can do,
I can do too.

389
00:20:46,933 --> 00:20:47,967
Sure!

390
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:49,733
Who can say no to those hands?

391
00:20:49,867 --> 00:20:50,933
Huh?

392
00:20:51,067 --> 00:20:52,333
Okay.

393
00:20:52,467 --> 00:20:53,733
Are you ready for your facial.

394
00:20:53,867 --> 00:20:55,933
- Shall we?
- Yes, come.

395
00:21:04,933 --> 00:21:06,000
Oh...

396
00:21:06,133 --> 00:21:07,933
Oh, he's already inside.

397
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:10,233
Nice.

398
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:22,267
My husband was imprisoned.

399
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:24,233
I thought I could handle it.

400
00:21:24,367 --> 00:21:27,333
May husband
is kind of well-connected.

401
00:21:27,733 --> 00:21:30,433
Would you like me to take a look
at your husband's case?

402
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:33,933
So if Golda used
to be a distributor,

403
00:21:34,067 --> 00:21:35,700
she may know people
in the syndicate

404
00:21:35,833 --> 00:21:37,433
like Theresa Park.

405
00:21:37,567 --> 00:21:38,467
If that's the case,

406
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:40,167
we'll be hitting two birds
with one stone.

407
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:42,267
But we still haven't
resolved one problem.

408
00:21:42,433 --> 00:21:43,333
It's Golda.

409
00:21:43,467 --> 00:21:44,667
She's slippery too.

410
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,767
Excuse me, where's Golda?

411
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:48,267
- Trigger! Trigger!
- Trigger! Trigger!

412
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:50,200
You've been staring at me
for a while now.

413
00:21:50,333 --> 00:21:51,100
Who are you?

414
00:21:51,233 --> 00:21:53,700
Do you know Ramon Orbos?

415
00:21:53,833 --> 00:21:54,867
How did you find me?

416
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,533
Who are you afraid of, Golda?

417
00:21:56,667 --> 00:21:57,767
I'm Miguel Delgado's daughter.

418
00:21:57,900 --> 00:21:59,967
Don't come any closer!
